Stop unzReadCurrentFile() looping forever on a truncated
bzip2-compressed zip entry, so the zip target stops timing out.

The bzip2 branch of unzReadCurrentFile() (src/main/dounzip.c) loops
while BZ2_bzDecompress() returns BZ_OK; once the entry's compressed
bytes are all consumed but the stream has not ended, the decoder keeps
returning BZ_OK with no output and the loop never terminates (inflate()
reports Z_BUF_ERROR in that state, so the deflate branch is fine).
Treat a call that produced no output with no input left as
BZ_UNEXPECTED_EOF.  Upstream minizip has the same bug.

The upstream PR also adds a regression test (tests/reg-tests-1e.R),
not carried here.

Found by OSS-Fuzz: testcase 4567145158344704 (libFuzzer_r_zip,
Timeout; readLines() over unz()).

Upstream status: r-devel/r-svn PR #372, filed 2026-10-10 (no Bugzilla
report yet).
Delete this patch once the fix lands in R trunk (ossfuzz.sh will report
it as already-applied in the meantime, which is harmless).

--- a/src/main/dounzip.c
+++ b/src/main/dounzip.c
@@ -2099,6 +2099,17 @@
 	      return (iRead == 0) ? UNZ_EOF : iRead;
 	    if (err != BZ_OK)
 	      break;
+	    /* BZ_OK with no output means the decoder wants more input.
+	       With the entry's compressed bytes all consumed there is
+	       none, so the stream is truncated and this loop would never
+	       end.  (inflate() reports Z_BUF_ERROR in that state.) */
+	    if (uOutThis == 0 &&
+		pfile_in_zip_read_info->stream.avail_in == 0 &&
+		pfile_in_zip_read_info->rest_read_compressed == 0)
+	    {
+		err = BZ_UNEXPECTED_EOF;
+		break;
+	    }
 #endif
 	} // end Z_BZIP2ED
 	else
